xz_32: xz (32-bit compression libraries based on the LZMA algorithm)
xz_32:
xz_32: LZMA is a general purpose compression algorithm designed by Igor
xz_32: Pavlov as part of 7-Zip.  It provides high compression ratio while
xz_32: keeping the decompression speed fast.  XZ Utils are an attempt to make
xz_32: LZMA compression easy to use on free (as in freedom) operating
xz_32: systems.
xz_32:
xz_32: The people most responsible for xz are Igor Pavlov, Ville Koskinen,
xz_32: and Lasse Collin.  For more info:  http://tukaani.org/xz/
